00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.590 align:start position:0%
european union ministers responsible for  energy policy aim this week to agree on  new rules to make the use of biofuels in  the eu more sustainable and so help cut  greenhouse gas emissions  the council wants to finalize its  position on so-called indirect land use  change this is when farmland is used to  produce biofuels leading to food or feed  being grown in other areas like forests  which results in more carbon dioxide in  the atmosphere the aim is to minimize  the environmental impact of indirect  land use and encourage more advanced  biofuels onto the market  also on the agenda the ministers are set  to endorse a report on progress made  toward completing europe's internal  energy market by next year's target days  the report addresses aspects like the  development of energy infrastructure  ensuring investments energy efficiency  and pricing  the council is also likely to endorse a  second report on the external dimension  of eu energy policy it covers  developments in the global energy  landscape in recent years progress made  in eu policies in this domain and looks  at ways to strengthen them
 

